@page "/about"

<PageTitle>About</PageTitle>

<div class="mt-2">
    <strong>About</strong>
    <hr class="mt-1" />
</div>
<p>
    The RSC Randomizer, also known as the Open RSC Randomizer, was a project created by me, Beast Fable.
    I thought it would be interesting one day to have a script randomize where NPCs spawn, and that idea
    eventually evolved into a real application. Initially, the randomizer was a .NET console application
    that you had to run on a Windows PC and it was rather clunky. Which is why it's now on the web, huzzah!
</p>
<p>
    In the future, I'd love to enhance this app to provide even more randomization possibilities, including
    randomized skilling scenery (e.g. mining rocks and fishing spots in random places) and randomized NPC
    drop tables. Imagine rune rocks being south of Varrock, or thugs dropping a Large Rune Helmet! Additionally,
    I'd like to eventually update this app to download the entire Core Framework project for you with the 
    randomized JSON files intact, so it's easier to get started for new users.
</p>